## Context
Child B of tracker 1045. Blocked by child A (the hook refuses an update of `main` that carries no gate record). Trap known in advance: this repository sets `core.hooksPath=hooks`, so a hook placed in `.git/hooks` never runs; a client that overrides `core.hooksPath` defeats the hook, which is why the sweep exists. Only git and the forge's API; no agent-runtime hook is the basis.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A `reference-transaction` hook journals every update of `main`: time, OS user, host, command lines of the process chain, git identity
- [ ] The hook refuses an update of `main` that is not a gated merge, verified from a second worktree; its installation is verified under `core.hooksPath`
- [ ] A periodic sweep checks that each commit that entered `main` is the merge of a PR whose required checks were green (or, once built, of a gate record) and reports any that is not
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime
- [ ] Catalog regenerated and drift check clean; PR under the 15-file breaker, else split
